1. Introduction
ALFAR AI, operated by Alfred Chamboko, develops Alfred Business Messenger AI Chatbot, an artificial intelligence chatbot designed to help businesses communicate with customers, answer questions, and provide information.

This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled while the chatbot is being developed, tested, deployed, and made available online through a public URL or supported messaging platform.

2. Information We Collect
Depending on the chatbot's features, we may process:

Names, email addresses, and phone numbers provided by users.
Messages and conversations with the chatbot.
Business enquiries and feedback.
Technical information needed to maintain security and performance.
Users should avoid sharing passwords, banking details, or sensitive personal information through the chatbot.

3. How We Use Information
Information may be used to:

Answer questions and assist customers.
Provide business information and support.
Test and improve chatbot functionality.
Fix errors and maintain security.
Maintain conversation history where necessary.
Operate and improve the online service.
4. Artificial Intelligence
Alfred AI uses artificial intelligence to understand messages and generate responses. Responses may sometimes be inaccurate and should be checked before being relied upon for important decisions.

If the chatbot uses third-party AI providers, messages may be processed by those providers to generate responses, subject to the applicable service arrangements and privacy terms.

5. Development and Public Access
During development and testing, information may be processed to check the chatbot's functionality and performance.

When the chatbot becomes publicly available through a URL, users may interact with it over the internet. We will take reasonable steps to secure the website, protect access to information, and prevent unauthorized access.

6. Data Sharing and Security
ALFAR AI does not intend to sell users' personal information.

Information may be processed by authorized hosting providers, AI services, messaging platforms, or technical service providers required to operate the chatbot.

We will take reasonable steps to protect information against unauthorized access, loss, or misuse. However, no online service can guarantee complete security.

7. Data Storage and Deletion
Information will be retained only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, subject to applicable legal requirements.

Users may contact us to request access to, correction of, or deletion of their personal information. Some records may need to be retained where legally required.

Deleting a message from a messaging platform may not automatically delete all copies stored by the chatbot or its service providers.

8. Third-Party Services
Alfred AI may depend on third-party messaging platforms, AI providers, databases, and hosting services. These providers may process information under their own privacy policies and terms.

Users should review the relevant third-party policies when using connected services.

9. User Privacy
Users may have rights to access, correct, or request deletion of their personal information, depending on applicable law.

Businesses using Alfred AI are responsible for ensuring they have the necessary authorization to share customer information with the chatbot.

10. Updates to This Policy
As Alfred AI develops and moves from testing to public launch, this policy may be updated to reflect new features, integrations, or changes in how information is handled.

The latest version should be available through the official chatbot website or public URL.

